    "name": "Spider curls",
    "content": "---\nexercise_name: Spider curls\nexercise_type: strength\ntags:\n- biceps\naliases:\n- Паучьи сгибания (Spider Curls)\ncategory: arms\ntier: 3\nrank_source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6g57DJntRXk\nvideo: https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=spider%20curl\nhelper_id: 57\n---\n\n# Spider curls\n\n**Better still** · [Biceps Exercises Ranked (BEST TO WORST!)](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6g57DJntRXk)\n\n**Target muscles:** Biceps\n\n## Starting position\n\nLie chest-down on an incline bench (45°). Let your arms hang straight down vertically, holding a barbell or dumbbells.\n\n## Step-by-step technique\n\n1. Bend your elbows to curl the weight, without letting your upper arm move out of the vertical position.\n\n## Key points\n\n- Peak biceps contraction at the top.\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- Letting your elbows drift back toward the bench.\n\n## 🛡️ Spine safety\n\nThe chest is supported, so the spine is protected; keep the neck neutral (look at the floor) and do not lift the chest off the bench.\n\n## 🛋️ At home, with what you have\n\nLie chest-down on the sofa arm or a stack of pillows on a chair; the dumbbells hang in front.\n\n## Video\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=spider%20curl\n"
