    "content": "---\nexercise_name: Low-to-high crossover (band)\nexercise_type: strength\ntags:\n- upper_chest\n- chest\naliases:\n- Сведение с резинкой снизу вверх (Low-to-High Crossover)\ncategory: chest\ntier: 4\nrank_source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YqFfh5IZUBs\nvideo: https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=low%20to%20high%20cable%20crossover\nequipment_band: true\nhelper_id: 74\n---\n\n# Low-to-high crossover (band)\n\n**Almost best** · [Upper Chest Exercises Ranked (BEST TO WORST!)](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YqFfh5IZUBs)\n\n**Target muscles:** Chest (upper chest)\n\n> [!warning] In the original this exercise uses a cable machine; here it is done with a resistance band.\n\n## Starting position\n\nThe bands are anchored low behind you. Stand in the center with your arms down at your sides and pulled back.\n\n## Step-by-step technique\n\n1. Exhale and bring your arms together in front of you in an arc from low to high, up to chin level.\n2. Squeeze your pecs at the top.\n\n## Key points\n\n- Isolates the upper chest.\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- Bending your arms at the elbows.\n\n## 🛡️ Spine safety\n\nStay tall with the ribs down; do not lean back or swing from the hips to pull the band up.\n\n## 🛋️ At home, with what you have\n\nAnchor two bands low on a door or use a loop band under the feet.\n\n## Video\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=low%20to%20high%20cable%20crossover\n"
